## Interview Context
This question evaluates your ability to drive technical change without formal authority—a critical competency for senior engineers and engineering managers who must lead through influence rather than position power.

## Key Concepts
- **Strategic Stakeholder Mapping**: Using RACI (Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed) matrices to systematically identify decision-makers, influencers, and blockers across the organization
- **Data-Driven Influence**: Leveraging quantitative evidence including A/B testing results, performance metrics, and business impact data to build compelling technical arguments
- **Technical Credibility Building**: Establishing authority through comprehensive documentation, working prototypes, and consistent delivery of high-quality technical solutions

